  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry weather continues under high pressure\n\nBig bubble is causing only minor forecast troubles. Plenty of\nsun and generally light wind into Sat. The main trouble is just\nhow low the dewpoints/RHs go each afternoon. Pattern recognition\nof mass fields and model soundings results in more-dry mixed- \nlayer each aftn than NBM mean would have us forecasting. Have\nkept continuity with lower-than-NBM dewpoints (closer to GFS\nMOS which is normally reliable on high pressure days) for the \nnext 3 aftns. We'll also keep the changes we've been making to \novernight temps, dropping them a couple of degs. \n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Light rain possible late Sun-Sun night\n\nSfc high slides off shore this weekend. A little ridge is left\nto arc back into the Appalachians. A sfc low developing in the\nBahamas has some tropical characteristics and could deepen well\nas it moves up the Gulf Stream this weekend. Good model\nconsensus on the western extent of rain from this low as it\ncontinues to moves poleward along the Gulf Stream. The back \nedge of the rain is painted over the Lower Susq with light rain\nthere for Sun-Sun night. The cold front concurrently moving \ninto PA will be losing all it's moisture, and may not even\ngenerate measurable RA for the western mtns. Best call right now\nis for a dry corridor over the middle third or more of the CWA\nin between anything the front can generate and the RA from the\ncoastal low.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3: Mixed precip possible around Thanksgiving Day\n\nSignals remain and seem to be increasing somewhat for mixed \nprecip to slide into the state from the south Wed or Thurs \n(Thanksgiving). Sfc low develops either off FL or somewhere in \nthe Deep South and rides north into the Mid-Atlantic. All the \nensembles have a 20-50pct chc of having >=0.25\" of liquid fall \nduring that period (Wed-Thurs) over PA, esp SE PA. Wet bulb \ntemps and 8H temps from several models are <=32F and 0C, \nrespectively - with colder air being pulled in from the west. \nNBM mean PoPs have increased to nearly 50pct for 0.01\" of \nprecip. We continue to mention a mix of precip over the \nALleghenies - and straight SN for Wed night. Mixed RA/SN also \nin there for almost all the rest of the CWA overnight with only \na small portion (again, the SE) going back to RA for Thurs aftn.\n\nThe deterministic 00Z/19th ECMWF run and the AIFS (EC) are\n/very/ bullish on precip with temps conducive to at least a mix\nfor the NW half of the CWA if not straight snow. In fact, the\nECMWF draws the deepening sfc low right over Harrisburg Thurs\naftn. GEFS plots are also pointing to mixed precip with a low\nmore on the coast or off-shore - but also at our latitude \nThurs. AI-GFS is almost devoid of precip for PA. Still Day 7 at\nthis point.",
